<title>USA: Duke sees Oconee 2 nuke at full output Wed.</title>
<headline>Duke sees Oconee 2 nuke at full output Wed.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duke Power Co said Tuesday its 846 megawatt (MW) Oconee 2 nuclear power plant in Seneca, S.C., will likely resume full output Wednesday after being shut Monday to repair a valve.</p>
<p>&quot;It went on line at 1135 (EDT). It's powering up...It's going to be a day or so to get up to full power,&quot; said company spokesman Rick Zuercher.</p>
<p>The neighboring Oconee units 1 and 3, also each rated at 846 MW, are producing at 100 percent of capacity.</p>
<p>Duke is the operator and sole owner of the Oconee units.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622</p>
</text>
